              "summary": "**Navigating NYC subway routes**\n\nI'm thinking about the routes for the D and F lines from Grand St to East Broadway. The D runs to the Manhattan Bridge, while the F goes through Broadway-Lafayette. There's a stop for the F at East Broadway on a separate track. If I take the F northbound to Delancey-Essex, I can transfer to the J train at Fulton St. However, I need to remember that the Bowery is closed on weekends, but the J still runs even if it bypasses that station!**Understanding subway transfers**\n\nI’m figuring out the route from East Broadway to Fulton St. It seems I'll transfer at Delancey-Essex. From East Broadway to Delancey-Essex is one stop, then I can stay on the J train to Fulton, which has stops at Bowery, Canal, and Chambers, totaling four stops. I'm curious if the transfers at Delancey-Essex are free since the F, M, and J lines share that stop. Alternatively, I could take the F to York St and transfer to the A/C at Jay St MetroTech.**Mapping the F/A/C route**\n\nI'm considering the F train route starting at East Broadway, stopping at York and Jay St-MetroTech. If I transfer to the A/C train at Jay, I can then go to High St and Fulton. Counting the stops, it looks like East Broadway to York is one, York to Jay is two, and then from Jay to High is three, followed by Fulton for a total of four stops. Alternatively, I could take the A/C directly from Jay to Fulton, which still adds up to four stops.",
